4. AUTOMATIC UPDATES

The Software contains an in-app updater that may download and
install future versions. You can disable automatic update checks in
Settings. Updates may add, change, or remove features.


5. PRIVACY

The Software collects only the data needed to deliver its features.
A summary of what is collected, how it is used, and how to exercise
Your rights (access, deletion, export) is in our Privacy Policy at
https://torve.app/privacy.

Crash and diagnostic reporting is optional and disabled by default
unless You consent during onboarding.


6. OPEN SOURCE COMPONENTS

The Software bundles open-source software, including VideoLAN's VLC
(libvlc, libvlccore, and the VLC plugin set), FFmpeg, libmpv (when
present in the runtime), Kotlin, kotlinx-coroutines, Jetpack Compose
for Desktop, Skiko, JNA, Ktor, SQLDelight, Sentry, and other
libraries listed in the project's dependency manifest.

Open-source components are licensed under their respective licenses.
Most are permissively licensed (Apache 2.0, MIT, BSD). VLC and its
plugin tree are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 2.1 ("LGPL-2.1"); the upstream license text is
included as `runtime/windows/vlc/COPYING.txt` in the installation
directory and can be re-read at any time.

Per the LGPL-2.1, You have the right to:

  - obtain the corresponding source code for the bundled VLC libraries
    (we ship the unmodified upstream binaries; the source is available
    from https://www.videolan.org/vlc/);
  - replace the bundled VLC libraries with your own version, by
    swapping the files in the installation's runtime directory;
  - re-link the Software against a modified VLC, subject to the
    LGPL-2.1's requirements.

Nothing in this Agreement restricts the rights granted by an
open-source license to its respective component.


